From: Peter Meiser <peter.meiser@gmx.com>
Subject: [PATCH] EGL Loader: prefer split software drivers over libGLES_android

The headless Biscuit has no vendor GLES blob. The previous fallback
returned /system/lib/egl/libGLES_android.so as soon as the combined
"GLES" lookup found nothing. Loader::open() asks for the combined
driver first, so libagl (GLES 1.x only) was always picked and a split
driver such as SwiftShader (libEGL_swiftshader.so,
libGLESv1_CM_swiftshader.so, libGLESv2_swiftshader.so) was never
tried.

Leave the combined lookup empty so Loader::open() goes on to the split
EGL/GLESv1_CM/GLESv2 lookup. Only when a split library is missing too,
fall back to libGLES_android.so, which exports all three APIs.

---
 opengl/libs/EGL/Loader.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/frameworks/native/opengl/libs/EGL/Loader.cpp
+++ b/frameworks/native/opengl/libs/EGL/Loader.cpp
@@ -413,6 +413,18 @@
             }
 
-            // we didn't find the driver. gah.
-            result.clear();
+            // ponytail: headless Biscuit has no vendor GLES blob.
+            // Leave the combined "GLES" lookup empty so Loader::open() tries
+            // the split EGL/GLESv1_CM/GLESv2 drivers (e.g. SwiftShader) next.
+            // Only if a split driver is missing too, use the source-built
+            // software renderer, which provides all three APIs.
+            if (!strcmp(kind, "GLES")) {
+                result.clear();
+                return result;
+            }
+#if defined(__LP64__)
+            result.setTo("/system/lib64/egl/libGLES_android.so");
+#else
+            result.setTo("/system/lib/egl/libGLES_android.so");
+#endif
             return result;
         }
